   "stem": {
      "text": "The density of suspended sediment in a vertical column of river water is modeled by \\( \\rho(h) = 12 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{h^{2}}{2} \\right)} + 30 \\) grams per cubic meter, where h is the depth below the surface in meters. Consider the column, which has horizontal cross-sections of constant area 4 square meters. Using a calculator, find the mass, in grams, of sediment in the column between the depths \\( h = 1 \\) and \\( h = 4 \\) meters. Show the setup, and give the value correct to three decimal places.",
      "setup_required": true,
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
