      "units": "grams"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A thin slab of thickness dh holds about \\( 4\\,\\rho(h)\\,dh \\), so the total is \\( 4\\int_{1}^{4} \\left(12 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{h^{2}}{2} \\right)} + 30\\right)\\,dh \\).",
         "rule_named": "accumulation of a density"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "With the calculator in radian mode the integral is about 98.926.",
         "mathjson": 98.92559247093145,
         "rule_named": "numerical integration"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Multiplying by the area 4 gives about 395.702.",
